Would you raid a colony whose last attackers are buried outside the walls?

RimWorld counts the silver behind those walls. Deterrence also counts what it costs to reach it. A colony with a dangerous approach or a fearsome reputation can face smaller raids. Your silver, buildings, and trade prices keep their usual value.

[h2]What makes a colony dangerous?[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Remains[/b] count while you keep them. Hostile bodies still count after burial. When a body is gone, its effect fades. Large graveyards count less per body as they grow. Locally harvested prisoner organs also count while they remain in stock.
[*][b]Reputation[/b] outlives the fight. Hostile deaths, prisoner surgeries, and executions add to a shared reputation that fades over time. With Ideology, you can also choose a reputation boost as a ritual reward.
[*][b]Hazards[/b] build up while the colony is dangerous. Toxic fallout, hostile hives, and extreme outdoor temperatures all contribute. When conditions improve, their effects gradually wear off.
[/list]

[h2]Who comes, and who turns back?[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Different outsiders fear different things.[/b] The Smart preset lets waster pirates ignore pollution and toxic hazards, insects ignore remains and reputation, and mechanoids ignore hazards. Faction settings also size infestations, mech clusters, and crashed ship parts.
[*][b]Raiders can think twice.[/b] Optionally, deterred raiders call off some raids, retreat after fewer losses as your reputation grows, and weigh their own dead more heavily.
[*][b]Safety can be lonely.[/b] Optionally, traders, visitors, travelers, and wanderers arrive less often at a deterred colony.
[*][b]Quests follow your choice.[/b] Quest threats and rewards can use the adjusted threat wealth or the game's own.
[/list]

[h2]See what changed[/h2]
Click the shield beside [b]World[/b]. The meters show your colony’s base and adjusted threat wealth, how much each source contributes, and how long fading effects will last. Expand a meter to inspect individual contributors. The History tab shows how the balance changed over time.

[h2]Make it fit your colony[/h2]
Tune the weights, growth, and fade times against a live graph. Adjust the effect of biomes and islands, or let different factions respond differently to the same colony. The Effects tab collects the optional raid, arrival, and quest settings. For burial, graves, sarcophagi, and stockpiles can filter humanlike corpses by status at death, current faction relations, or faction name.

[b]Requirements[/b] — RimWorld 1.6 and Harmony. The core mod works without DLC. Biotech adds pollution, Royalty adds the psychic droner and toxic spewer, and Ideology adds the optional ritual reward. Existing Antiwealth saves and settings are supported.

